Patches to @pierre/diffs, applied by bun (package.json "patchedDependencies").
Bun ignores everything above the first "diff --git" line, so keep notes here.
`bun patch` regenerates this file when committing, so copy this header back afterwards.

When upgrading @pierre/diffs, check each part below against the new version and drop only
the parts it fixes. Test in the Files editor with wrap long lines turned on (the default),
using a markdown file that has many long, wrapping lines.

1. CodeView.js: skip layout while the root is hidden (isRootHidden)
   Bug: while the editor is display: none (Source/Rendered toggle, or another work-view tab
   in front), CodeView's ResizeObserver still renders and caches every wrapped line as 0px.
   The zeros stay after the editor shows again, so the wrong lines or a blank gap appear at
   the top, and the caret can't get into that gap.
   Can be dropped once both of these start at line 1, with no gap, and the caret moves up
   to line 1:
   - Open a .md file (it opens in Rendered), then choose Source.
   - In Source, switch to another tab, resize the window, then switch back.
   Without this hunk, `__INSTANCE.items[0].instance.cache.heights` in the console has lines
   cached as 0 after either step; with a fixed upstream it has none.

2. editor.js: ignore the echo of our own window selection (#windowSelectionEcho,
   getComposedWindowRange, isSameRange)
   Bug: a late selectionchange from the editor's own setBaseAndExtent is read as a click,
   collapsing the selection to its anchor.
   Can be dropped once holding Shift+Arrow (all four directions, including across wrapped
   lines) keeps extending the selection without it collapsing.

3. editor.js: mirror the whole selection natively (#focus's `selection` argument)
   Bug: the native selection is collapsed at the anchor, so clicking the anchor after
   Shift+Arrow is a no-op and the selection stays.
   Can be dropped once: select with Shift+Arrow, then click exactly where the selection
   started, and the selection clears.

4. selection.js: Up on the first line goes to the line start, Down on the last line goes to
   the line end (mapCursorMove, moveBySoftLine)
   Can be dropped once Up on line 1 jumps the caret to the start of the document and Down
   on the last line jumps to the end, with and without Shift and on wrapped lines too.

